The Eberhard grocery advertisement from the January 12, 1977, edition of *The North Kent Leader* has been deconstructed into an immersive, first-person social media feed. 

Using the **Rashomon Effect**, I broke the advertisement down into 7 distinct entries:
- **First-Person Posts:** Perspectives from the "Friendly Ad-Visor" regarding coupon savings and the "Eberhard Store Manager" on community value.
- **Targeted Ads:** Specific promotional updates for the meat department (Wilson's Certified Steaks), household essentials (Charmin), frozen goods (Morton Dinners), and the Polly Anna Bakery.

The resulting JSON file has been saved to `temp/North%20Kent%20Leader%20-%2001-12-1977%20-%20Page%204.json`.
